content.text:
The `mongodb-recommendation` memory shift is a drop, not a rise, and `recommendation`'s own spans are unchanged, so it is not a second fault. I have enough to answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, count(*) n, min(value) min_v, max(value) max_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='geo' AND metric IN ('k8s.deployment.available','k8s.deployment.desired') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "geo deployment shows 0 available pods against 1 desired throughout the abnormal window"},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, max(value) max_restarts FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'geo-%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "geo container restart counter climbs to 6 in the abnormal window; the pod kept being killed and recreated"},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('geo.Geo/Nearby') GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "geo.Geo/Nearby server spans are absent in the abnormal period; normal period has 1161"},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "search's client calls to geo.Geo/Nearby almost all fail: 1133 of 1137 have error status in abnormal period"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "geo", "to": "search",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name IN ('search.Search/Nearby','geo.Geo/Nearby') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "search's own Nearby server spans fail with error status, 1133 of 1137, after its geo calls fail"}]},
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "frontend HTTP /hotels requests fail with error status, 1099 of 1103, because search failed"}]}
  ]
}
```
